      "created_at": "2017-04-21T19:57:51.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Thanks for the feedback, folks, is really helpful <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"dpt\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dpt/48/1922_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> dpt:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Your text is very nicely gender-neutral, and I appreciate that the two roles are not particularly gendered (particularly with the coffee+socialite combination). Is there a way to tweak the card backs?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yeah, I’ve tried really hard to avoid gendering what are very gender-able roles. What do you see as wrong with the card backs?</p>",
